silm:instances_papers_07_the_canonical_question_chapters_08_cross_paper_bridges_sections_05_bridge_to_11_base_commutative_concrete_anchor_3#mittenssourcediagram silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensSourceDiagram is the source diagram D_Mittens with ten typed cocone legs gluing into the Mittens apex. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_{\\Mittens}', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
